{"id":"mahabharata-6-008","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":8,"title":"अष्टमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 8 · Northern lands and Mount Meru","summary":{"en":"Sanjaya describes the lands north and east of Meru, the holy Uttarakuru country and its blessed people. He tells of the mountains Malyavat and Nila and the lands beyond.","kn":"ಮೇರುವಿನ ಉತ್ತರ ಮತ್ತು ಪೂರ್ವ ಪ್ರದೇಶಗಳನ್ನು, ಪುಣ್ಯಭೂಮಿ ಉತ್ತರಕುರು ಹಾಗೂ ಅಲ್ಲಿಯ ಭಾಗ್ಯಶಾಲಿ ಜನರನ್ನು ಸಂಜಯನು ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಮಾಲ್ಯವತ್ ಮತ್ತು ನೀಲ ಪರ್ವತಗಳ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"संजय मेरु के उत्तर और पूर्व के प्रदेशों, पवित्र उत्तरकुरु देश और वहाँ के सौभाग्यशाली लोगों का वर्णन करते हैं। वे माल्यवान और नील पर्वतों तथा उनसे परे के देशों की बात करते हैं।","te":"మేరువుకు ఉత్తర, తూర్పు ప్రాంతాలను, పుణ్యభూమి ఉత్తరకురు దేశాన్ని, అక్కడి భాగ్యవంతులైన ప్రజలను సంజయుడు వర్ణిస్తాడు. మాల్యవంతం, నీల పర్వతాలు, వాటి అవతల దేశాల గురించి చెబుతాడు.","ta":"மேருவின் வடக்கு, கிழக்குப் பகுதிகளையும் புண்ணிய உத்தரகுரு நாட்டையும் அங்குள்ள பாக்கியசாலிகளையும் சஞ்சயன் விவரிக்கிறான். மால்யவான், நீல மலைகளையும் அப்பாலுள்ள நாடுகளையும் கூறுகிறான்.","ml":"മേരുവിന്റെ വടക്കും കിഴക്കുമുള്ള ദേശങ്ങളെയും പുണ്യമായ ഉത്തരകുരു രാജ്യത്തെയും അവിടത്തെ അനുഗൃഹീതരായ ജനങ്ങളെയും സഞ്ജയൻ വിവരിക്കുന്നു. മാല്യവാൻ, നീലം എന്നീ പർവതങ്ങളെക്കുറിച്ചും അപ്പുറത്തുള്ള ദേശങ്ങളെക്കുറിച്ചും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.8; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"जम्बूखण्डविनिर्माणपर्व","titleEn":"Jambukhandavinirmana Parva (Description of Jambudvipa)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"मेरोरथोत्तरं पार्श्वं पूर्वं चाचक्ष्व संजय ।\nनिखिलेन महाबुद्धे माल्यवन्तं च पर्वतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, now tell me fully, great-minded one, of the northern and eastern sides of Meru and of the mountain Malyavan."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"दक्षिणेन तु नीलस्य मेरोः पार्श्वे तथोत्तरे ।\nउत्तराः कुरवो राजन्पुण्याः सिद्धनिषेविताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"South of Nila, on the northern flank of Meru, King, lie the holy Northern Kurus, frequented by Siddhas."}},{"n":3,"text":"तत्र वृक्षा मधुफला नित्यपुष्पफलोपगाः ।\nपुष्पाणि च सुगन्धीनि रसवन्ति फलानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the trees bear honey-sweet fruit and always have flowers and fruit; the flowers are fragrant and the fruits full of flavour."}},{"n":4,"text":"सर्वकामफलास्तत्र केचिद्वृक्षा जनाधिप ।\nअपरे क्षीरिणो नाम वृक्षास्तत्र नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of the people, some trees there yield every desire; others there, lord of men, are the trees called Kshirins."}},{"n":5,"text":"ये क्षरन्ति सदा क्षीरं षड्रसं ह्यमृतोपमम् ।\nवस्त्राणि च प्रसूयन्ते फलेष्वाभरणानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"They always drip milk with six flavours, like nectar, and their fruits produce garments and ornaments."}},{"n":6,"text":"सर्वा मणिमयी भूमिः सूक्ष्मकाञ्चनवालुका ।\nसर्वत्र सुखसंस्पर्शा निष्पङ्का च जनाधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"The whole ground is made of gems with fine golden sand, pleasant to the touch everywhere and free of mud, lord of the people."}},{"n":7,"text":"देवलोकच्युताः सर्वे जायन्ते तत्र मानवाः ।\nतुल्यरूपगुणोपेताः समेषु विषमेषु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Human beings born there have all fallen from the world of the gods, alike in form and quality, whether the ground is level or uneven."}},{"n":8,"text":"मिथुनानि च जायन्ते स्त्रियश्चाप्सरसोपमाः ।\nतेषां ते क्षीरिणां क्षीरं पिबन्त्यमृतसंनिभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are born as pairs, and the women are like Apsarases; they drink the milk of the Kshirin trees, which is like nectar."}},{"n":9,"text":"मिथुनं जायमानं वै समं तच्च प्रवर्धते ।\nतुल्यरूपगुणोपेतं समवेषं तथैव च ।\nएकैकमनुरक्तं च चक्रवाकसमं विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Each pair grows up together, alike in form, quality and dress, and each is devoted to the other like a pair of chakravaka birds, mighty king."}},{"n":10,"text":"निरामया वीतशोका नित्यं मुदितमानसाः ।\nदश वर्षसहस्राणि दश वर्षशतानि च ।\nजीवन्ति ते महाराज न चान्योन्यं जहत्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are free of sickness and sorrow, always cheerful, and live eleven thousand years, great king, without ever leaving one another."}},{"n":11,"text":"भारुण्डा नाम शकुनास्तीक्ष्णतुण्डा महाबलाः ।\nते निर्हरन्ति हि मृतान्दरीषु प्रक्षिपन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"There are birds called Bharundas, with sharp beaks and great strength, who carry off the dead and throw them into caves."}},{"n":12,"text":"उत्तराः कुरवो राजन्व्याख्यातास्ते समासतः ।\nमेरोः पार्श्वमहं पूर्वं वक्ष्याम्यथ यथातथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus I have briefly described the Northern Kurus, King; now I will describe truthfully the eastern side of Meru."}},{"n":13,"text":"तस्य पूर्वाभिषेकस्तु भद्राश्वस्य विशां पते ।\nभद्रसालवनं यत्र कालाम्रश्च महाद्रुमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of the people, in its east lies Bhadrashva, with the forest Bhadrasala and the great tree Kalamra."}},{"n":14,"text":"कालाम्रश्च महाराज नित्यपुष्पफलः शुभः ।\nद्वीपश्च योजनोत्सेधः सिद्धचारणसेवितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, the Kalamra is auspicious and always bears flowers and fruit; the island is a yojana high and frequented by Siddhas and Charanas."}},{"n":15,"text":"तत्र ते पुरुषाः श्वेतास्तेजोयुक्ता महाबलाः ।\nस्त्रियः कुमुदवर्णाश्च सुन्दर्यः प्रियदर्शनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the men are white, full of vigour and very strong, and the women, lovely and pleasing to see, are the colour of white lotuses."}},{"n":16,"text":"चन्द्रप्रभाश्चन्द्रवर्णाः पूर्णचन्द्रनिभाननाः ।\nचन्द्रशीतलगात्र्यश्च नृत्तगीतविशारदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They shine like the moon, have the colour of the moon, faces like the full moon and bodies cool as the moon, and are skilled in dance and song."}},{"n":17,"text":"दश वर्षसहस्राणि तत्रायुर्भरतर्षभ ।\nकालाम्ररसपीतास्ते नित्यं संस्थितयौवनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of the Bharatas, their life there is ten thousand years; they drink the juice of the Kalamra and keep their youth forever."}},{"n":18,"text":"दक्षिणेन तु नीलस्य निषधस्योत्तरेण तु ।\nसुदर्शनो नाम महाञ्जम्बूवृक्षः सनातनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"South of Nila and north of Nishadha stands the great eternal rose-apple tree called Sudarshana."}},{"n":19,"text":"सर्वकामफलः पुण्यः सिद्धचारणसेवितः ।\nतस्य नाम्ना समाख्यातो जम्बूद्वीपः सनातनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is holy, yields every desire and is frequented by Siddhas and Charanas; Jambudvipa, the eternal, is named after it."}},{"n":20,"text":"योजनानां सहस्रं च शतं च भरतर्षभ ।\nउत्सेधो वृक्षराजस्य दिवस्पृङ्मनुजेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of the Bharatas, lord of men, the king of trees is eleven hundred yojanas high, touching the sky."}},{"n":21,"text":"अरत्नीनां सहस्रं च शतानि दश पञ्च च ।\nपरिणाहस्तु वृक्षस्य फलानां रसभेदिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Its girth is fifteen hundred and a thousand cubits, and its fruits burst with juice."}},{"n":22,"text":"पतमानानि तान्युर्व्यां कुर्वन्ति विपुलं स्वनम् ।\nमुञ्चन्ति च रसं राजंस्तस्मिन्रजतसंनिभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Falling on the ground they make a great sound, and they let out a juice, King, that is like silver."}},{"n":23,"text":"तस्या जम्ब्वाः फलरसो नदी भूत्वा जनाधिप ।\nमेरुं प्रदक्षिणं कृत्वा संप्रयात्युत्तरान्कुरून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The juice of that rose-apple fruit becomes a river, lord of the people, and after circling Meru to the right it flows to the Northern Kurus."}},{"n":24,"text":"पिबन्ति तद्रसं हृष्टा जना नित्यं जनाधिप ।\nतस्मिन्फलरसे पीते न जरा बाधते च तान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The people there always drink that juice happily, and having drunk the fruit juice, old age does not trouble them."}},{"n":25,"text":"तत्र जाम्बूनदं नाम कनकं देवभूषणम् ।\nतरुणादित्यवर्णाश्च जायन्ते तत्र मानवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is the gold called Jambunada, an ornament of the gods, and the people there are born with the colour of the young sun."}},{"n":26,"text":"तथा माल्यवतः शृङ्गे दीप्यते तत्र हव्यवाट् ।\nनाम्ना संवर्तको नाम कालाग्निर्भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"On the peak of Malyavan there blazes the fire that carries oblations, called Samvartaka, the fire of time, best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":27,"text":"तथा माल्यवतः शृङ्गे पूर्वे पूर्वान्तगण्डिका ।\nयोजनानां सहस्राणि पञ्चाशन्माल्यवान्स्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Malyavan, fifty thousand yojanas in extent, lies on the eastern edge of the eastern range."}},{"n":28,"text":"महारजतसंकाशा जायन्ते तत्र मानवाः ।\nब्रह्मलोकाच्च्युताः सर्वे सर्वे च ब्रह्मवादिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"People born there look like great silver; all have fallen from the world of Brahma and are all speakers of Brahman."}},{"n":29,"text":"तपस्तु तप्यमानास्ते भवन्ति ह्यूर्ध्वरेतसः ।\nरक्षणार्थं तु भूतानां प्रविशन्ति दिवाकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Practising austerities they become men of retained seed, and to protect beings they enter the sun."}},{"n":30,"text":"षष्टिस्तानि सहस्राणि षष्टिरेव शतानि च ।\nअरुणस्याग्रतो यान्ति परिवार्य दिवाकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sixty thousand and sixty hundred of them go ahead of Aruna, encircling the sun."}},{"n":31,"text":"षष्टिं वर्षसहस्राणि षष्टिमेव शतानि च ।\nआदित्यतापतप्तास्ते विशन्ति शशिमण्डलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For sixty thousand years and sixty hundred, scorched by the sun's heat, they then enter the orb of the moon."}}]}]}